# Input Sanitization (Node.js)

Concepts: see `../../patterns/input-sanitization.mdc`. Below: API-specific.

## Validation vs Sanitization

- **Validation:** Reject invalid input (format, range)
- **Sanitization:** Transform to safe form (escape, strip tags, normalize path)
- Use both at API boundary

## SQL Injection

- Use parameterized queries only (ORM or prepared statements); never concatenate user input into SQL
- Prisma/Drizzle/TypeORM use parameters by default; avoid raw query with string interpolation

## XSS

- For APIs returning data to browser: frontend must escape; if API returns HTML, sanitize with DOMPurify or allowlist on server before storing
- Validate Content-Type and size for file uploads; store with safe names

## Path Traversal

- Validate file paths; do not use user input directly in fs.readFile(path); resolve to canonical path and check it is under allowed root
- For URLs: validate protocol (http/https); allowlist domains if building URLs from input

## Conventions

- Validate at boundary (Zod + refinements); sanitize before persist or output; use allowlist over blocklist
- Log validation failures without logging full input (could be sensitive)

## Anti-Patterns

- Raw SQL with input; trusting client path or URL; no max length/size; storing unsanitized HTML

